=$" :question/worked-solution "This integral doesn't look like one of the basic ones. However, we can manipulate the numerator a bit  to make it look more like the denominator, which reveals a more familiar expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{2{x}^{3}+2x+1}{{x}^{2}+1} & =\\frac{2x({x}^{2}+1)+1}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\cancel{({x}^{2}+1)}}{\\cancel{{x}^{2}+1}}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =2x+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRemembering that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C,\n$$\n\nwe can now calculate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x)=\\int {f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int x\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-71779/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e6b5d85-0b53-580f-9520-6c33463231d5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71779"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186064456 :question/answer-fields 17592186061385] {:db/id "q-19102/selection/ma-v1/0eb0c638a8cb0685d39cc7855d957e02b06cbf7ed475777fd6fd538a5002954c/d19b73a3ffd0046f0474ec2e9e7805295f0aae708cab65a31f2bc85fd5487088" :answer/id #uuid "d551847f-21ca-5319-b70c-9efa450bee70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,\\text{arccos}\\,x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19102/selection/ma-v1/0eb0c638a8cb0685d39cc7855d957e02b06cbf7ed475777fd6fd538a5002954c/4c4e76d7262a1e490e4dddea9869a7353a6379a42f76f5b9560ed182497d7d4a" :answer/id #uuid "1b10c492-700a-5a6a-8925-cd9c75ff3066" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x-3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19102/selection/ma-v1/0eb0c638a8cb0685d39cc7855d957e02b06cbf7ed475777fd6fd538a5002954c/5c2f4