bf7ed475777fd6fd538a5002954c/28e7bef0a37839fc8405ef7032ef0953082f1012650a243b1fc0c1538b5cfcae"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-19102"] :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "This integral doesn't look like one of the basic ones. However, we can manipulate the numerator a bit  to make it look more like the denominator, which reveals a more familiar expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+1} & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}+3-3}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3({x}^{2}+1)-3}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3({x}^{2}+1)}{{x}^{2}+1}-\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cancel{({x}^{2}+1)}}{\\cancel{{x}^{2}+1}}-\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =3-\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRemembering that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,\n$$\n\nwe can now calculate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3-\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\text{d}x-3\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3x-3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-19102/selection/ma-v1/0eb0c638a8cb0685d39cc7855d957e02b06cbf7ed475777fd6fd538a5002954c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-114184/selection/44650d7ff08908d8bebbf257babf40abee09a5230af4cd4a10582232e4d8b1af" :answer/id #uuid "300f5dad-723b-516a-b2a6-5a33970eeb26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114184/selection/22092a5bcb0fa8bc8a93a712ab5264fbfa9a14267f71119638b2eeb77c7e70db" :answer/id #uuid "4da3833f-efe1-59ce-a7a0-1617319d8b72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x+4\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114184/selection/bf0a77c1eed32a6030be999e264c1c107f48628340245baba393eb5e